.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux-expand 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux\-expand \- Expand a snippet template, e.g. "Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux expand\fR [\fB\-\-arg\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITEMPLATE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Expand a snippet template, e.g. "Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}"
.PP
Prints TEMPLATE with its {variables} replaced. Fails if a variable is unknown or an {arg:NAME} has no matching \-\-arg.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-arg\fR \fI<NAME=VALUE>\fR
A value for {arg:NAME}; repeat for several parameters
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fITEMPLATE\fR>
Text with {variables} to expand; quote it to keep the braces from the shell
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
\fB{date}\fR
Today\*(Aqs date as YYYY\-MM\-DD.
.TP
\fB{date:FORMAT}\fR
The current time in any strftime(3) FORMAT, for example {date:%A %d %B}.
.TP
\fB{time}\fR
The current time as HH:MM.
.TP
\fB{clipboard}\fR
The clipboard\*(Aqs text, or nothing if it is empty.
.TP
\fB{arg:NAME}\fR
The value given with \-\-arg NAME=VALUE.
.TP
\fB{{ and }}\fR
A literal { or }.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Fill in parameters:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux expand \*(AqHi {arg:name}, re: {arg:topic}\*(Aq \-\-arg name=Sam \-\-arg topic=Invoices\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Values with spaces need quotes:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux expand \*(AqHi {arg:name}\*(Aq \-\-arg \*(Aqname=Sam Lee\*(Aq\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quote the clipboard with a timestamp:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux expand \*(Aq> {clipboard} ({date} {time})\*(Aq\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\fR(1), \fBstrftime\fR(3)
